                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Jane's Realty is terribly unbalanced for such a short game. You will start out with levels that can literally be won in seconds. Place a building or two and mission accomplished. At the end, you are given such absurdly difficult goals you will wonder if the game designers were trying to make the game unplayable (they certainly made it unenjoyable). There are very few levels to play, and time runs out quickly per level. The bulk of the game is actually spent replaying previous levels so that you will have resources you need to pass later levels.\n\nIf you like repetition and being frustrated, here's your game. If not, spend your three dollars elsewhere.",
